algorithms.pseudocode:
function GramEncode(a, b, c):
    return [[a² + b², a² + b·c],
            [a² + b·c, a² + c²]]

Complexity: O(1) arithmetic operations

function AncestryRecover(a, b, c):
    word ← []
    while (a, b, c) ≠ (3, 4, 5):
        for g in {L, M, R}:
            parent ← B_g⁻¹(a, b, c)
            if parent is valid and B_g(parent) = (a,b,c):
                word.prepend(g)
                (a,b,c) ← parent
                break
    return word

Complexity: O(depth) = O(log c) expected
